# The information a character sheet set must carry before anything is drawn from it
law avatar_sheet
kind sheet
claim a sheet set is several pages: the turnaround, the base body, the face, the hair, each clothing layer, accessories and footwear, the materials and the palette; each page is drawn from these slots and the avatar laws, never from a free drawing
claim lengths are in the units of the avatar laws (the body: the eye height above the sole is 1; the face: the chin-to-eye distance is 1) unless a slot names another unit
claim a slot is filled with a value of its type inside its range or vocabulary; a required slot left empty, a value out of range, a reference to nothing or a file without provenance is listed by the check, and no page is drawn until every required slot of the set is filled
claim pending marks a slot that exists here before the part law that should own it as a knob has it
uses avatar_body body.law
uses avatar_face face.law

page turnaround: the body from the front, the side and the back at one scale, standing on one ground line, with guide lines at the landmark heights and the joints marked
slot turnaround.stature number unit m range 0.5 2.5 required source knob:body.stature pending body : height from the sole to the top of the skull, without hair
slot turnaround.pose enum vocab T|A required source authored pending skeleton : arms straight out (T) or lowered (A)
slot turnaround.arm_angle number unit deg range 0 60 required when pose=A source authored pending skeleton : angle of the arms below the horizontal
slot turnaround.views enum vocab front_side_back required source authored : the three views drawn
slot turnaround.joint_marks bool required source authored : the elbows, wrists, hip joints, knees and ankles are marked (they cannot be read from a silhouette)

page base_body: the body's proportions, in eye heights above the sole
slot base_body.hips_y number unit eye_height range law avatar_body.hips_y required source law:avatar_body.hips_y : height of the hips
slot base_body.hip_drop number unit eye_height range law avatar_body.hip_drop required source law:avatar_body.hip_drop : the hip joints below the hips
slot base_body.hip_x number unit eye_height range law avatar_body.hip_x required source law:avatar_body.hip_x : the hip joint's distance from the centre line
slot base_body.knee number unit eye_height range law avatar_body.knee required source law:avatar_body.knee : height of the knee joint
slot base_body.shoulder_x number unit eye_height range law avatar_body.shoulder_x required source law:avatar_body.shoulder_x : the shoulder joint's distance from the centre line
slot base_body.arm number unit eye_height range law avatar_body.arm required source law:avatar_body.arm : shoulder to wrist
slot base_body.elbow_split number unit fraction range law avatar_body.elbow_split required source law:avatar_body.elbow_split : the elbow's place along the arm, from the shoulder
slot base_body.face_length number unit eye_height range law avatar_body.face_length required source law:avatar_body.face_length : the chin below the eyes
slot base_body.head_top number unit eye_height range law avatar_body.head_top required source law:avatar_body.head_top : the top of the skull, without hair

page face: the face from the front and the side, in chin-to-eye distances, and its expressions
slot face.eye_width number unit chin_eye range law avatar_face.eye_width required source law:avatar_face.eye_width : width of one eye
slot face.eye_height number unit chin_eye range law avatar_face.eye_height required source law:avatar_face.eye_height : height of one eye
slot face.eye_recess number unit chin_eye range law avatar_face.eye_recess required source law:avatar_face.eye_recess : how far the eyes sit behind the front of the face
slot face.brow_y number unit chin_eye range law avatar_face.brow_y required source law:avatar_face.brow_y : height of the brows
slot face.brow_inner number unit chin_eye range law avatar_face.brow_inner required source law:avatar_face.brow_inner : the inner end of a brow from the centre line
slot face.brow_outer number unit chin_eye range law avatar_face.brow_outer required source law:avatar_face.brow_outer : the outer end of a brow from the centre line
slot face.mouth_y number unit chin_eye range law avatar_face.mouth_y required source law:avatar_face.mouth_y : height of the mouth
slot face.mouth_width number unit chin_eye range law avatar_face.mouth_width required source law:avatar_face.mouth_width : width of the mouth
slot face.depth number unit chin_eye range law avatar_face.depth required source law:avatar_face.depth : depth of the head, front to back
slot face.eye_colour ref palette.colours.name required source authored : the iris colour
group face.expressions min 1 max 16 : expressions drawn on the face page
field face.expressions.name enum vocab neutral|smile|laugh|surprise|anger|sad|shy|wink|closed required source authored pending face : one expression
field face.expressions.note text max 80 optional source authored : what is particular about it

page hair: the hair's style, where it is tied, its length and its strands
slot hair.style_class enum vocab short|bob|long_straight|long_wavy|ponytail|twin_tails|bun|braid required source authored pending hair : the kind of hair style
slot hair.length number unit eye_height range 0.05 1.2 required source authored pending hair : the longest strands' length below the top of the skull
slot hair.parting number unit deg range -40 40 required source authored pending hair : the parting's angle from the centre (0 = centred)
slot hair.fringe enum vocab none|short|eyebrow|eye_covering required source authored pending hair : how far the fringe falls (eye_covering hides the brows: the face page then marks them)
slot hair.curl_amplitude number unit mm range 0 15 required source authored pending hair : 0 for straight hair
slot hair.curl_pitch number unit mm range 20 200 required when curl_amplitude>0 source authored pending hair : length of one turn of a curl
slot hair.colour ref palette.colours.name required source authored : the hair's colour
group hair.ties min 0 max 4 : where bundles are gathered (ponytail, twin tails, bun)
field hair.ties.height number unit fraction range 0 1 required source authored pending hair : height on the head, from the nape (0) to the crown (1)
field hair.ties.azimuth number unit deg range -180 180 required source authored pending hair : around the head, 0 = the back, positive = the figure's left
field hair.ties.length number unit eye_height range 0.02 1.2 required source authored pending hair : length of the gathered bundle
field hair.ties.accessory ref accessories.items.name optional source authored : what ties it

page clothing: each clothing layer, from the skin outwards
group clothing.layers min 0 max 8 : one layer of clothing
field clothing.layers.name text max 40 required source authored : a name for the layer (unique)
field clothing.layers.order int range 1 8 required source knob:garment.layer_order : the layer's place from the skin outwards (1 = on the skin)
field clothing.layers.class enum vocab skin|loose|chain|rigid required source authored pending garment : skin = follows the body, loose = drapes, chain = a hem or ribbon that swings, rigid = a hard part
field clothing.layers.from enum vocab head_top|chin|shoulder|elbow|wrist|hips|hip_joint|knee|ankle|sole required source authored pending garment : the landmark the layer starts at
field clothing.layers.to enum vocab head_top|chin|shoulder|elbow|wrist|hips|hip_joint|knee|ankle|sole required source authored pending garment : the landmark the layer ends at
field clothing.layers.hem number unit fraction range 0 1 required source authored pending garment : where the hem falls between from (0) and to (1)
field clothing.layers.ease number unit mm range 0 200 required source authored pending garment : the gap between the layer and what is under it
field clothing.layers.closure enum vocab none|buttons|zip|laces|hooks|wrap required source authored pending garment : how it is closed
field clothing.layers.material ref materials.items.name required source authored : what it is made of

page accessories: accessories and footwear, at their absolute size, attached to the body
group accessories.items min 0 max 16 : one accessory or one piece of footwear
field accessories.items.name text max 40 required source authored : a name for the item (unique)
field accessories.items.kind enum vocab footwear|ribbon|hair_ornament|jewellery|bag|hat|gloves|other required source authored pending accessory : what it is
field accessories.items.attach enum vocab head_top|chin|shoulder|elbow|wrist|hips|hip_joint|knee|ankle|sole|hair_tie required source authored pending accessory : the landmark it is attached at
field accessories.items.size number unit mm range 1 1000 required source authored pending accessory : its largest dimension
field accessories.items.sole number unit mm range 0 100 required when kind=footwear source authored pending accessory : thickness of the sole under the ball of the foot
field accessories.items.heel number unit mm range 0 150 required when kind=footwear source authored pending accessory : how far the heel lifts the heel of the foot
field accessories.items.material ref materials.items.name required source authored : what it is made of

page materials: what every part is made of and how light passes through it
group materials.items min 1 max 24 : one material
field materials.items.name text max 40 required source authored : a name for the material (unique)
field materials.items.class enum vocab fabric|leather|metal|skin|hair|plastic|paper|glass|other required source authored pending material : the kind of material
field materials.items.colour ref palette.colours.name required source authored : its base colour
field materials.items.roughness number unit fraction range 0 1 required source knob:material.roughness : 0 = mirror-smooth, 1 = fully rough
field materials.items.metallic number unit fraction range 0 1 required source authored pending material : 0 = not metal, 1 = metal
field materials.items.shade_shift number unit fraction range -1 1 required source knob:toon.shift : where the shadow edge falls (toon shading)
field materials.items.shade_softness number unit fraction range 0 1 required source knob:toon.toony : 0 = soft shadow edge, 1 = hard
field materials.items.outline number unit mm range 0 5 required source knob:toon.outline.width : outline width (0 = none)
field materials.items.transmission enum vocab opaque|open_weave|diffuse|clear required source authored pending material : how light passes through it
field materials.items.openness number unit fraction range 0 1 required when transmission=open_weave source authored pending material : share of light passing straight through the weave
field materials.items.thread_colour ref palette.colours.name required when transmission=open_weave source authored pending material : colour of the threads
field materials.items.thickness number unit mm range 0.01 10 required when transmission=open_weave source authored pending material : thickness of the cloth
field materials.items.stretch_sensitivity number unit fraction range 0 1 optional when transmission=open_weave source authored pending material : how much the weave opens when stretched
field materials.items.transmittance number unit fraction range 0 1 required when transmission=diffuse source authored pending material : share of light passing through, scattered
field materials.items.scattering number unit fraction range 0 1 required when transmission=diffuse source authored pending material : how much what is behind blurs (1 = only a glow)
field materials.items.ior number unit ratio range 1 3 required when transmission=clear source authored pending material : index of refraction
field materials.items.tint ref palette.colours.name optional when transmission=clear source authored pending material : the colour it tints what is behind
field materials.items.pattern enum vocab none|procedural|texture required source authored : how its surface varies
field materials.items.pattern_law text max 80 required when pattern=procedural source authored : the material law that draws the pattern
field materials.items.texture asset required when pattern=texture source authored : the image file of the pattern or print
field materials.items.used_by text max 200 required source authored : which parts use it (layer and accessory names, skin, hair, eyes)

page palette: the named colours every page refers to
group palette.colours min 1 max 32 : one named colour
field palette.colours.name text max 40 required source authored : a name for the colour (unique)
field palette.colours.srgb colour required source authored : the colour as #rrggbb in sRGB

text allow law_values : every number, name and unit drawn on a page is a filled slot's value or a value of the laws the sheet uses (with its unit)
text allow page_titles : the page names of this law and the slots' names as labels
text forbid tool_names : no tool, product, engine, file format or law name drawn on a page (the sheet shows the character, not how it is made)
text forbid unsourced_claims : no technical claim that no slot or law states (file size, precision, polygon or point counts, data formats, model kinds)
text forbid other_proportion_units : no proportion in units the laws do not use (heads tall, a height of 1) and no proportion number that is not a slot's value
rule unique clothing.layers.name : layer names differ
rule unique clothing.layers.order : no two layers in one place
rule unique accessories.items.name : item names differ
rule unique materials.items.name : material names differ
rule unique palette.colours.name : colour names differ
rule unique face.expressions.name : each expression is drawn once
rule ordered clothing.layers.from clothing.layers.to : a layer starts above where it ends (landmarks from the top of the head down)
